ent flag, re-run printing exactly (37, 27, 0) and (24823, 7945, 0).** Checker-side alarms honestly recorded (all the reviewer's own, re-run green): a K₄ union-before-test checker bug (the per-edge augment re-run 38/463/0), a first defect-2 demo instance that didn't trigger (redesigned), a brute-force that forgot a sink arc, two MemoryLimitError runs whose writes had already landed (verified on disk after), and a shell frontmatter count artifact resolved at close (the head/wc pipeline collapses the title's em-dash, undercounting by 2 — the TS byte view is authoritative: 166,469 = 158 frontmatter + 166,310 payload + 1 trailing newline exactly). Rebuild rule executed: the appendix gained the "Adversarial review (session 69)" record + an editions-paragraph sentence + the footer's "+ adversarial review (session 69)" extension; hygiene green post-edit (fences 16 balanced, mojibake 0, no session references before the appendix); the web edition rebuilt with fidelity proof first (the old payload's re-render byte-exact against the old .html by the port — one convergence rule added this session, `> ` blockquote lines); codec round-trip green (the TS extraction byte-faithful: 166,469 = 158 + 166,310 + 1; the independent shell base64 -d of the spliced MD_B64 md5-equal to the payload); payload 162,843 chars / 166,310 bytes (b64 221,748, mod 4 = 0, line 49), frame untouched, web canvas + web master both 228,113 B at the 138-line convention (canvas == master, diff -q ✓); .html rebaked 168,657 → 176,924 B, no script, no MD_B64, the write-back gate green (the .html == head + renderMd(new payload) + tail exactly). Chapter master == canvas: 1,230 lines / 166,469 B (1,225 lines / 158,264 B pre-review). Canvas drift caught and fixed at open (the chapter canvas had lost its trailing newline — the session-44 drift class — resynced from the master before review). Chapter-map row 11's history extended (review session 69) + stats refreshed. Masters synced: cgt-ch11-algorithms.md, cgt-ch11-web