- **Session 67 — the adversarial review arc continued: Ch. 9 (Sumsets and Shadows: the Completed Arcs) reviewed COMPLETE (two arguing experts — the skeptic and the engineer — chunk by chunk, for correctness, coherence, exposition, and figure aid; extend, never rewrite; every retained objection machine-verified before any edit).** Ch. 9 verdict: mathematics otherwise CLEAN — a fresh exhaustive battery re-verified every checkable claim green (deep censuses: (6,3) deep = 42 = complete with 0 violations / 0 equality candidates; (6,4) deep = 22 = complete, 0/0; (7,5) pin = 29 = complete (21 K⁵₅ + 7 K⁵₆ + 1 K⁵₇), deep = pin via the §4.2 corollary (noted honestly, not recounted); the [6] bonus census exactly 57 equality families (15 single edges, 20 triangles, 15 K₄, 6 K₅, 1 K₆), 0 violations; mirror arithmetic exact everywhere: (9,4) 56 + 70 = 126, (5,2) 4 + 6, (7,3) 15 + 20, (8,3) 21 + 35, h(t) = [6, 21, 56, 126] with h(8) = C(9,4); the ten-edge hunt over 352,716 graphs with the t-distribution [2961, 18480, 78120, 126210, 85260, 33054, 6300, 2310, 0, 0, 21] — 2,310 at t = 7, none at 8/9, the 21 at t = 10 all with degree pattern 0,0,4,4,4,4,4 (K₅ + 2 isolated), the per-vertex ceilings K(v) ≤ 10 − d(v) and K(v) ≤ (3/2)d(v) zero violations; the (9,4) hunt UPGRADED FROM HONEST BUDGET TO PROOF — a branch-and-bound max-clique search with the core-emptiness constraint (WLOG A = {0,1,2,3}, the killability prune, the coloring bound) exhausted in 6,374 nodes: no empty-core intersecting 4-family on [9] reaches 54, the maximum is 53 = Hilton–Milner exactly, the HM family verified (53 sets, pairwise intersecting, core ∅), four sanity-target validations before the negative result was trusted (finds 53 with a core, 54/56 without, nothing at 57 → the EKR star = 56); cross-refs valid (P4's reverse rows Ex16/20, P22's Ex17, P23's Ex19; Ex11/Ex18's lore hints; Ch. 6's multilinear lemma §3.1, Ch. 7's ◐15/complementary-pair/circle-method/shifting pointers, Ch. 8's equitable-quotient theorem)